    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "Oregon Institute of Technology: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.oit.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Oregon Institute of Technology: All Jobs 2026-07-22T13:07:28-07:00 https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7453 2026-07-22T13:07:27-07:00 2026-07-22T13:07:28-07:00 Assistant Professor <div>Oregon Institute of Technology, a premier public polytechnic university in the Pacific Northwest, and the Electrical Engineering and Renewable Energy Department (EERE) invite applications for the position of Assistant Professor. Oregon Tech is one of the top public regional universities in the western United States and is consistently ranked among the top public universities in the nation by US News &amp; World Report. Oregon Tech offers innovative and rigorous degree programs.<br><br></div><div>The job responsibilities for the Assistant Professor position include teaching courses (with labs) in microcontrollers, digital systems, control systems, among other areas. Additionally, candidates should be enthusiastic about innovations in instruction, curriculum development, and student engagement. The successful candidate must have expertise in one or more of the following electrical engineering areas such as digital systems, chip design, and intelligent and autonomous systems (AI/machine learning, robotics). Outstanding candidates from other areas are also encouraged to apply. Candidates for this position are expected to develop externally funded applied research programs and projects involving students on applied research. Other responsibilities include advising students, directing student projects, and participating in continuous professional development, as well as other departmental and institutional service activities.</div> Electrical Eng & Renewable Energy https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7073 2025-08-08T11:10:04-07:00 2025-08-08T11:10:04-07:00 Adjunct Instructor, Globalization <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Adjunct Instructors to teach online sections of Globalization for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br></div><div>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions to support the department's General Education courses, including Globalization. The course is taken by a range of Oregon Tech students and is required for programs in engineering, business, and social sciences.<br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in-person on-campus, hybrid, or related lab; or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div><strong>Location: </strong>The primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.<br><br>Interested candidates should apply to the posting through the posting on the Oregon Tech Job Board, and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7459 2026-07-28T14:49:38-07:00 2026-07-28T14:49:39-07:00 Administrative Program Specialist <div>The Administrative Program Specialist (Clinic Manager) works under the direction of the Clinic Director to provide essential managerial support to the Associate Clinic Director, students, and other staff. The Clinic Manager will coordinate daily operations for BRIDGE Center. Duties of this position include:<br>1. Providing quality customer service, interfacing with patients, doctors offices, vendors, and staff<br>2. Ensuring the clinic follows all legal and regulatory processes for insurance billing and other reimbursement<br>3. Clinic operations related to day to day management of appointments, phone calls, emails and other inquiries<br>4. Budget management, scheduling, purchasing, inventory, etc.</div> Behavioral Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7075 2025-08-08T11:23:19-07:00 2025-08-08T11:23:19-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Public Health & Population Health <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Public Health and Population Health undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br></div><div>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions for the minor in Medical Sociology and undergraduate degree in Population Health Management. Specifically, the department seeks adjunct instructors to teach Medical Sociology, Introduction to Population Health Management, Global Population Health, Rural Health, Current Health Issues, Community Program Planning, among others.<br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div><strong>Location:</strong> primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.</div><div><br>Interested candidates should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/4412 2021-08-04T16:07:55-07:00 2021-08-04T16:07:56-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Humanities <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Humanities Undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences Department.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Humanities and Social Sciences Department at the Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time adjunct teaching positions for our humanities courses (ethics, humanities, literature, philosophy). Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses within the department.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises as early as September 2021. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br></div><div>Teaching Modality: Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div>Location: primary campus locations include Klamath Falls, OR, Wilsonville, OR and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online.&nbsp;</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7476 2026-08-18T12:57:43-07:00 2026-08-18T12:57:43-07:00 Sponsored Projects Financial Manager <div>The Sponsored Projects Financial Manager (SPFM) is a key partner in the financial and administrative management of externally funded projects from proposal development to closeout. This position is responsible for - financial management of awards, provides strategic financial oversight of OIT’s sponsored projects portfolio, ensures compliance with sponsor and institutional requirements, and supports principal investigators (PIs) and departments in effectively managing sponsored project resources. The position works closely with Business Affairs Office (BAO) grant accounting to prepare and monitor grant related accounting transactions. The position is responsible for the financial management of grants and sponsored projects, including ensuring compliance with Federal and State laws and regulations, the rules and regulations of funding agencies, the terms and conditions of grants/awards, as well as Oregon Tech policies and procedures.<br><br>In addition, this position is responsible for preparation and submission of required financial reports and other progress and activity reports as required by sponsoring agencies. The Sponsored Projects Financial Manager (SPFM) works with BAO grant accounting to ensure that invoices are submitted in a timely fashion and that supporting documentation is accurate and properly recorded. The SPFM advises principal investigators, faculty and administrators on fiscal matters as they relate to grants and contracts; performing various analysis, developing special reports, as needed, and providing faculty training on grant budget development and management. The SPFM maintains accurate and complete financial and administrative documentation for sponsored projects and serves as a resource for accurate and complete information on grants and contracts cost preparation and post award administrative and financial support to principal investigators, project directors and sponsors.<br><br>The position reports to the Director for Sponsored Projects and Grants Administration, while working collaboratively to manage the cost preparation and post-award administration and management of grants. The position will also work collaboratively with the University Development Office and the university Foundation to assist in development-funded projects.<br><br>Through collaboration with the Assistant Director of the Business Affairs Office (BAO), the SPFM ensures all grants/projects are set up in the University financial system according to the sponsor-approved budget guidelines, cost sharing companion accounts are established to segregate expenditures and that grant close-outs are performed in accordance with written University procedures. The SPFM also maintains fiscal records and reports required for cost sharing to sponsors.<br><br>This position will be located onsite at one of Oregon Tech's campuses. Campus location is negotiable between Portland-Metro (Wilsonville, OR) and Klamath Falls.</div> Grants & Sponsored Research https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7077 2025-08-08T11:27:59-07:00 2025-08-08T11:27:59-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Literature <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Literature undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions. Hired Adjunct Instructors would be teaching courses that help our students complete their General Education Humanities requirement for graduation; which are also part of our Arts, Literature, and Philosophy minor curriculum. Specifically, the department seeks adjunct instructors to teach: Introduction to Literature; Introduction to the Humanities; Medical Humanities; Technology, Society, and Values; American Literature, among others. <br><br><strong>Teaching Modality: </strong>Appointments may include courses offered online, in person on campus in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements .<br><br><strong>Location:</strong> The primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.<br><br>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify the areas you are qualified to offer courses in and/or the specific courses you would be interested in teaching.<br><br>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7492 2026-08-31T08:42:54-07:00 2026-08-31T08:42:54-07:00 Residence Life Coordinator <div>Oregon Tech Housing and Residence Life is seeking a vibrant and enthusiastic Residence Life Coordinator (RLC) to join the Housing and Residence Life team. The RLC serves as a key member of the Residence Life team in support of the mission, vision and values of the Housing and Residence Life department and Oregon Tech.<br><br>This employee works closely with the Lead Residence Life Coordinator, student staff, and residential students daily. The work includes developing community within all housing facilities to ensure a safe and welcoming environment for residential students as well as the campus community, families and guests who interact with Housing and Residence Life.<br><br>The RLC also supports and participates in Housing and Residence Life sponsored and supported programming in support of student learning initiatives. This position supervises the First Year Experience (FYE) student staff as well as the Student Success Mentor (SSM) staff team, reporting to the Assistant Director of Residence Life.<br><br>This position works Monday through Friday as well as some evenings and weekends. The RLC also serves in the on-call rotation to respond to Housing and Residence Life related emergency/crisis needs after hours and on weekends. A willingness and desire to work with students as they live and learn in a residential setting is essential as well as a strong work ethic to ensure the student experience while on campus and at Oregon Tech is one filled with positive learning experiences in a safe and inclusive environment.<br><br>The RLC is a live in position, with a fully furnished apartment and Meal Plan 3 included in the compensation.</div> Housing https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/5317 2022-08-22T10:23:08-07:00 2022-08-22T10:23:08-07:00 Adjunct Math Instructor <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Math Adjunct Instructors for the Department of Mathematics. This pool is created for an anticipated opening for winter term 2022, as well as for any future part-time adjunct faculty appointments. Appointment availability will vary from quarter to quarter as a function of student enrollment.&nbsp;<br><br>The primary purpose of this position is to teach 100 to 400 level mathematics classes. Duties include providing quality instructions for on-campus, daytime classes, performing grading and relevant preparation and maintaining appropriate records. The successful candidate will work with other faculty, staff, and administration to deliver an integrated learning experience in mathematic courses and will be available to teach classes on a variety of days and times.&nbsp;<br><br>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.</div><div>Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br></div><div>Teaching Modality: These classes will be principally in-person, with some online components possible. Instruction will include classroom lectures.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Location: This position will be at Oregon Tech’s Klamath Falls campus.</div> Mathematics https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7089 2025-08-22T11:01:44-07:00 2025-08-22T11:01:44-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Applied Psychology <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Psychology Undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences Department.</div><div>Humanities and Social Sciences Department at the Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time adjunct teaching positions for our Applied Psychology program. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses within the department.</div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br></div><div>Teaching Modality: Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div>Location: primary campus locations include Klamath Falls, OR, Wilsonville, OR and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7499 2026-09-03T16:50:32-07:00 2026-09-03T16:50:32-07:00 Administrative Program Assistant <div>This position provides administrative and program support for the Computer Systems Engineering and Electrical Engineering Technology (CSET) and Electrical Engineering &amp; Renewable Energy (EERE) programs within the College of Engineering, Technology and Management (ETM).<br><br>Responsibilities include administering departmental purchasing, travel, reimbursement, student organization funding, budget-related activities, records management, accreditation support, and event planning necessary to support program operations and services. The position serves as a primary administrative resource for faculty, students, external stakeholders, and university partners by administering established processes, facilitating communication, maintaining records, and supporting program delivery.</div><div><br>Work is performed with considerable independence in organizing assignments, managing competing priorities, coordinating recurring program activities, and completing administrative assignments from initiation through completion, receiving direction from the program department chairs. Duties require in-depth knowledge of the assigned programs and the application of established university, departmental, and regulatory requirements.</div><div><br>Using established procedures and criteria, the incumbent administers departmental purchasing, travel, reimbursement, and student organization funding processes, coordinates approvals, monitors compliance requirements, and resolves procedural issues to ensure assigned work progresses to completion. Final authority for budget decisions, policy interpretation, and matters outside established guidance remains with the department chair and applicable budget authorities.</div> General Instruction https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/5710 2023-02-21T12:37:43-08:00 2023-02-21T12:37:43-08:00 Adjunct Instructor - Information Technology (online) <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Undergraduate Adjunct Instructors in Information Technology for the Department of Management.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Management at the Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time adjunct teaching positions. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses across the Information Technology program including, C#.NET, Python, SQL Server, Windows Server, Systems Analysis Methodologies, big data methodologies, and data analytics.<br><br></div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises as early as April 2023. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br></div><div>Teaching Modality: Appointments may include courses offered on-line or in person on campus.<br><br></div><div>Location: Campus locations include Klamath Falls, OR and online</div> Management https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7183 2025-11-19T09:17:05-08:00 2025-11-19T09:17:05-08:00 Adjunct Instructor - Applied Behavior Analysis <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Applied Behavior Analysis Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences Department.<br><br></div><div>Humanities and Social Sciences Department at the Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time adjunct teaching positions for our undergraduate and graduate Applied Behavior Analysis programs. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses within the department.<br><br></div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/6260 2024-02-08T16:02:07-08:00 2024-02-08T16:02:07-08:00 Adjunct Instructor- Management <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Adjunct Instructors within the Department of Management.<br><br>The Department of Management at the Oregon Tech (Oregon Institute of Technology) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible Adjunct teaching positions. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses within the department.<br><br>Candidates interested in Adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching, from the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Accounting</li><li>Business Management</li><li>Cybersecurity&nbsp;</li><li>Health Care Management</li><li>Health Informatics</li><li>Information Technology</li><li>Leadership</li><li>Marketing</li><li>Operations Management - Quality Management and Lean Six Sigma experience &amp; credentials required</li><li>Technology &amp; Management&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br><strong>Teaching Modality: </strong>Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.In your cover letter, please note the location(s) you are available to teach from:</div><ul><li>On campus, Klamath Falls</li><li>On campus, Portland-Metro&nbsp;</li><li>Online</li></ul> Management https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7315 2026-03-03T17:05:10-08:00 2026-03-03T17:05:10-08:00 Adjunct Instructor, Communication Studies <div>The College of Health, Arts, and Sciences at Oregon Tech is seeking enthusiastic and well-qualified teachers for adjunct teaching positions to begin Spring term, April 2026 in Klamath Falls campus teaching accelerated four-week courses at an off-site location serving military students at Kingsley Field.<br><br></div><div>We are looking for instructors who could teach one or more of the following courses:</div><div>· Communication Software</div><div>· Intercultural Communication</div><div>· Essentials of Grammar and Punctuation</div><div>· Interpersonal Communication</div><div>· Digital Media Production</div><div>· Intro to Communication</div><div>· Intro to Leadership</div><div>· Communication Technology in Use</div><div>· Gender and Communication</div><div>· Communication Research</div><div>· Organizational Communication I and II</div><div>· Negotiation and Conflict Resolution</div><div>· Training and Development</div><div>· Communication and Leadership</div><div>· Small Group and Team Communication</div><div>· Writing in the Air Force<br><br></div><div>The Communication Department is committed to inclusive thought and action in support of our diverse community. Individuals from historically underrepresented groups and all those who share our commitment to inclusivity and passion for the strength of our diversity are strongly encouraged to apply.<br><br>Successful candidates will be required to complete a military background check prior to employment.</div> Communication https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/6486 2024-07-31T08:19:59-07:00 2024-07-31T08:19:59-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Marriage and Family Therapy <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences Department.</div><div><br>Humanities and Social Sciences Department at the Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time adjunct teaching positions for our MS in Marriage and Family Therapy program. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses within the department.<br><br></div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises as early as August 2024. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br></div><div>Teaching Modality: Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div>Location: HSS Department primary campus locations include Klamath Falls, OR, Wilsonville, OR and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7385 2026-05-05T12:26:12-07:00 2026-05-05T12:26:12-07:00 Instructor of Medical Imaging <div>The Medical Imaging Technology (MIT) department at Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) seeks applicants for an instructor which is a career track, full-time, nine-month position.<br><br>Oregon Tech is a public university located in Klamath Falls, Oregon. Klamath Falls is located in the foothills of the Cascade Mountains in southern Oregon and is known as Oregon’s City of Sunshine. It is widely recognized for its remarkable mountain and lake scenery, including Crater Lake National Park and year-round outdoor recreation opportunities. Klamath Falls is a small but vibrant town rich with arts and culture, downtown eateries, and craft breweries.<br><br>The MIT department offers a Bachelor of Science degree in five modalities: Diagnostic Medical Sonography, Echocardiography, Nuclear Medicine, Radiologic Science, and Vascular Technology. The Diagnostic Medical Sonography, Echocardiography and Vascular Technology modalities are CAAHEP accredited. All modalities emphasize student-centered instruction oriented towards professional success. Facilities provide state-of-the-art imaging equipment, labs, simulators, and the latest technology to prepare learners to be leaders in the field. The medical imaging faculty are an amazing team and part of a tradition of excellence at Oregon Tech.<br><br>The MIT department has faculty openings in four modalities. The Radiologic Science program seeks applicants with registries in CT, MRI and/or Interventional radiography. The Nuclear Medicine program seeks applicants holding certification in Nuclear Medicine from the ARRT or NMTCB. The Diagnostic Medical Sonography program seeks applicants with registries in breast, musculoskeletal, pediatrics and fetal echo. The Echocardiography program seeks applicants with registries in adult and pediatric echo.<br><br>The primary focus of all faculty positions in the MIT department is on excellent teaching at the bachelor’s level. The successful candidate’s instructional responsibilities will include a variety of core courses in one of the modalities depending upon certification/credentials, and experience. Faculty are expected to advise students, improve courses through continuous assessment, and adjust content to reflect current workforce trends.<br><br>Faculty are expected to pursue professional development to stay current in the discipline and enhance instructional practices. Faculty will participate in service activities for the institution (department and university levels), profession, and community.<br><br>We are pleased to offer competitive incentives to the successful candidate upon hire. Additional information will be provided to the selected candidate.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS<br>The position requires a master’s degree in medical imaging, higher education, or related field with a bachelor’s degree in a medical imaging modality. *Applicants hired without a master’s degree will be expected to earn a master’s degree within a time determined at hire. Applicants should have current certification/credentials and five years of related occupational work experience. Applicants should indicate modality preferred based upon certification/credentials, and experience in their cover letter.</div> Medical Imaging Technology https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/6928 2025-05-07T16:14:25-07:00 2025-05-07T16:14:26-07:00 Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing & Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) <div>The Department of Manufacturing and Mechanical Engineering Technology at Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is seeking applications for a part-time adjunct faculty pool for the 2025-2026 academic year. These positions will be based at the Portland-Metro campus in Wilsonville and will be offered on a term-by-term basis. Renewals may be considered annually at the discretion of the department chair.<br><br></div><div>Adjunct faculty will be responsible for developing and/or teaching undergraduate courses within the Manufacturing and Mechanical Engineering Technology department, which is part of the College of Engineering, Technology, and Management at Oregon Tech.<br><br></div><div>Courses that may require instructors include:<br><br></div><ul><li>Automation and Robotics</li><li>Programmable Logic Controllers (PLCs)</li><li>Control Systems</li><li>Materials Science and Engineering</li><li>Mechanical Vibrations</li><li>Electric Power Systems</li><li>Machining Processes</li><li>Manufacturing Tool Design</li><li>Computer-Aided Design (CAD) / Computer-Aided Manufacturing (CAM)</li></ul> Manufacturing & Mechanical Eng Tech https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7428 2026-06-11T10:35:04-07:00 2026-06-11T10:35:04-07:00 Student Involvement & Belonging Coordinator <div>The Student Involvement &amp; Belonging (SIB) Coordinator creates and supports a holistic student experience responsible for supporting the vision, initiatives, programs, and daily operations for Klamath Falls students. The SIB Coordinator will co-lead Klamath Falls campus Student Involvement &amp; Belonging programs and initiatives; collaborating with partners across the university campus to ensure a student0centered approach to the creation and implementation of programming that enhances a student’s sense of belonging and increases student’s leadership development and cultural competency.<br><br>The SIB Coordinator will use research, data, and assessment to lead the university in developing and implementing a co-curricular journey in which student’s belonging and leadership development experience will be enhanced. The SIB Coordinator is responsible for the Klamath Falls student involvement and campus activities through providing advising and support for Registered Student Organizations, creating Klamath Falls campus-wide student engagement opportunities, such as large-scale social events including Music Garden. The SIB Coordinator will develop, student leadership and cultural competency development, and diversity and belonging programming; and support the operations and programming of Student Involvement &amp; Belonging in collaboration with the Director of SIB and Assistant Director of SIB (Portland-Metro).<br><br>Student Involvement &amp; Belonging provides programs and services students need to achieve academic, personal, and professional goals. We provide programs, services, and partners with other divisions to provide support, enhance personal wellness, develop leadership and communication skills, and promote a strong sense of community. We encourage students to get involved on campus, approach faculty and staff with ideas, questions and concerns and take advantage of the resources that will help them succeed.</div> Student Involvement & Belonging https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7072 2025-08-08T11:06:52-07:00 2025-08-08T11:06:53-07:00 Adjunct Instructor, History <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for History undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions to support the department's General Education courses. Specifically, the department seeks adjunct instructors to teach: Intro to History, History of Medicine, History of Energy, Globalization, among others.<br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in-person on-campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab; or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div><strong>Location: </strong>The primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.</div><div><br></div><div>Interested candidates should apply to the posting through the posting on the Oregon Tech Job Board, and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7458 2026-07-28T14:41:35-07:00 2026-07-29T15:39:11-07:00 Assistant Professor - ABA <div>Oregon Institute of Technology is conducting a search for a full-time, tenure-track, 9-month faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Our new colleague will support our MS-ABA, BS-Applied Psychology, and BRIDGE Clinic programs. Responsibilities include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses, providing clinical supervision of students and other duties at the BRIDGE clinic. Applied research and excellence in instruction are expected of tenure track faculty at Oregon Tech. Service to the department, institution, and community are also highly valued.<br><br>The position reports to the Chair of the Behavioral Sciences department and the Director of the Building Resilience, Independence, Development, Growth, and Excellence Applied Behavior Analysis (BRIDGE ABA) clinic, who is responsible for assignment and evaluation of clinic-related activities.<br><br>Qualified candidates will have a doctoral degree in Psychology, Applied Behavior Analysis or related field from an accredited college or university and Board Certification in Behavior Analysis. Qualified candidates should demonstrate the ability to teach a broad range of classes that support our current curriculum. Oregon Tech offers competitive salaries and an excellent benefits package. Salary is commensurate with experience.<br><br>The MS in Applied Behavior Analysis and BS in Applied Psychology programs are housed within the Humanities and Social Sciences Department, a dynamic and growing department with a commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. Oregon Tech’s primary mission is teaching and our Applied Psychology and Applied Behavior Analysis programs have a strong practical component.<br><br>Candidates must be student-oriented and able to teach smaller seminar and lab classes with a hands-on emphasis, as well as larger lecture classes.</div> Behavioral Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7074 2025-08-08T11:11:22-07:00 2025-08-08T11:11:22-07:00 Adjunct Instructor, Sociology <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Sociology undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br></div><div>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions to support the department's General Education courses, minor in Medical Sociology, and undergraduate degree in Population Health Management. Specifically, the department seeks adjunct instructors to teach Introduction to Sociology, Social Problems, Medical Sociology, Aging and Society, Global Population Health, among others.<br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in-person on-campus, hybrid, or related lab; or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div><strong>Location: </strong>The primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.<br><br></div><div>Interested candidates should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7475 2026-08-18T12:29:04-07:00 2026-08-18T12:29:04-07:00 Information Technology Consultant 2 <div>This position provides application, hardware, and classroom/AV technology support for students, faculty, staff, and administration. It engages in evaluation of new technology and the planning, testing, training, and implementation necessary for successful organizational adoption. This position serves as a collaborative participant in Information Technology Services (ITS) technology decisions regarding end-user applications. This position is highly self-directed and relies heavily on the judgment necessary for independent decision making with critical attention to the customer relationship.</div> Information Technology Services https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7076 2025-08-08T11:24:35-07:00 2025-08-08T11:24:35-07:00 Adjunct Instructor, Philosophy <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Philosophy undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br></div><div>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions to support the department's General Education courses and minor in Arts, Literature, and Philosophy. Specifically, the department seeks adjunct instructors to teach HUM125: Technology, Society, and Values; PHIL331: Ethics in the Professions, and PHIL342: Business Ethics, among others. <br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br><strong>Location: </strong>The primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.<br><br></div><div>Interested candidates should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/5272 2022-08-01T13:07:03-07:00 2022-08-01T13:07:03-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Social Sciences - Klamath Falls <div>This position will support our Medical Sociology minor and Population Health Management program with coursework in Medical Sociology, Global Health, Research Methods, Current Health Issues, Program Planning, and/or Intro to Sociology.</div><div>Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses within the department.</div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br>This position will be in person on our Klamath Falls campus.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises as early as September 2022. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br></div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7491 2026-08-31T08:40:52-07:00 2026-08-31T08:40:52-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Dental Hygiene <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Adjunct Instructors for the Dental Hygiene department.<br><br></div><div>The department of Dental Hygiene is recruiting a pool of Adjunct Instructors for possible part-time teaching positions.<br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong>Adjunct Instructors of Dental Hygiene will be expected to complete in-person/on-campus instruction and/or related in-person/on-campus clinic or labs.<br><br></div><div><strong>Location:</strong>The Klamath Falls, OR, campus.</div><div><br>Interested candidates should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Dental Hygiene https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7078 2025-08-08T12:04:17-07:00 2025-08-08T12:04:17-07:00 Adjunct Instructor, Art and Design <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Art and Design undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br></div><div>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions to support the department's General Education and minor in Arts, Literature, and Philosophy courses. Specifically, the department seeks adjunct instructors to teach: Introduction to Drawing, Watercolors, Design and Aesthetics, Introduction to Graphic Design, Art History and other courses within the instructor’s field of expertise. <br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br><strong>Location: </strong>The primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.<br><br></div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7493 2026-08-31T08:43:56-07:00 2026-08-31T08:43:56-07:00 Healthcare Leadership Adjunct Instructor <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Adjunct Instructors in our<a href=\"https://www.oit.edu/online/degrees/master-of-science-healthcare-leadership\"><strong>Master of Healthcare Leadership Program</strong></a>. Qualified instructors have the opportunity to teach graduate-level courses in healthcare leadership, leadership theory, interdisciplinary healthcare leadership, healthcare ethics, and health policy. We welcome energetic, creative individuals with a desire to enhance and develop innovative courses that integrate the most current challenges and strategies for successful leadership in this era. This can include a wide variety of teaching methods and course materials beyond a typical textbook, such as videos, podcasts, social media, expert interviews, and connections to professional associations. Our program culture prioritizes student wellbeing, with professors serving as mentors, and opportunities for real world projects and reflections. <br><br><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> All courses are online and asynchronous. <br><br><strong>Location:</strong> Appointments are all remote positions affiliated with Oregon Tech’s online campus<br><br>Interested candidates should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be enthusiastic in teaching.</div><div><br>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/5481 2022-11-10T09:15:19-08:00 2022-11-10T09:15:19-08:00 Adjunct Instructor of Physical Therapy <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Adjunct Instructors for both the foundational sciences portion and the clinical sciences portion of the curriculum.</div><div>The program is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time adjunct teaching positions. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses within the program.</div><div>Candidates interested in adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but for no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br></div><div><strong>Teaching Modality</strong>: Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div><strong>Location</strong>: primary campus location is Klamath Falls, OR.</div> Physical Therapy https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7144 2025-10-27T14:57:50-07:00 2025-10-27T14:57:50-07:00 Adjunct Instructor Pool (Mathematics) <div>Oregon Tech Portland Metro is seeking Mathematics Instructors to teach lower division courses, specifically an in-person section of MATH 112 this Winter quarter with the possibility of future courses.The Portland-Metro campus is located in Wilsonville, OR.</div> Mathematics https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/5760 2023-03-15T10:51:23-07:00 2023-03-15T10:51:24-07:00 Adjunct Instructor - Information Technology <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Adjunct Instructors to teach undergraduate information technology courses for the Department of Management.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Management at the Klamath Falls campus of Oregon Tech (Oregon Institute of Technology) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time Adjunct teaching positions. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as instructors for courses across the Information Technology program including, C#.NET, Python, SQL Server, Windows Server, Systems Analysis Methodologies, big data methodologies, and data analytics.</div><div><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed when an opening or need arises as early as April 2023. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Management https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7241 2025-12-29T12:06:25-08:00 2025-12-29T12:06:26-08:00 Administrative Coordinator <div>Under the direction of the Manufacturing and Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) Department Chair, the Coordinator will support the development of global engagement programs at Oregon Tech.<br><br>The Coordinator is responsible for a broad array of office, technical, and administrative or business-related duties in support of campus programs and operations.<br><br>This part-time (0.50 FTE) position requires in-person reporting to the Seattle/Boeing campus, located at 2615 West Casino Road, Suite 2A, Everett, WA 98204, from 12:00 PM to 4:00 PM, Monday through Friday, or as directed.</div> Manufacturing & Mechanical Eng Tech https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/6268 2024-02-22T09:32:56-08:00 2024-02-22T09:32:56-08:00 Adjunct Instructor of Manufacturing, Mechanical Engineering and Technology <div>Oregon Tech is Accepting Applications for Undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Department of Manufacturing, Mechanical Engineering and Technology.<br><br>The Department of Manufacturing, Mechanical Engineering and Technology (MMET) at Oregon Tech (Oregon Institute of Technology) is recruiting a pool of persons for possible part-time Adjunct teaching positions. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as Adjunct Instructors for courses within the department.<br><br>Candidates interested in Adjunct teaching positions should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br>Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.<br><br>Teaching Modality: Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in person on campus, hybrid, or related clinic or lab, or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br>Location: MMET primary campus locations include Klamath Falls, OR, Wilsonville, OR and Everett, WA. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online depending upon the Departmental need and course requirement(s).</div> Manufacturing & Mechanical Eng Tech https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7384 2026-05-05T12:24:05-07:00 2026-05-05T12:24:06-07:00 Assistant Professor of Medical Imaging <div>The Medical Imaging Technology (MIT) department at Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) seeks applicants for a tenure track, Assistant Professor of Medical Imaging.<br><br>Oregon Tech is a public university located in Klamath Falls, Oregon. Klamath Falls is located in the foothills of the Cascade Mountains in southern Oregon and is known as Oregon’s City of Sunshine. It is widely recognized for its remarkable mountain and lake scenery, including Crater Lake National Park and year-round outdoor recreation opportunities. Klamath Falls is a small but vibrant town rich with arts and culture, downtown eateries, and craft breweries.<br><br>The MIT department offers a Bachelor of Science degree in five modalities: Diagnostic Medical Sonography, Echocardiography, Nuclear Medicine, Radiologic Science, and Vascular Technology. The Diagnostic Medical Sonography, Echocardiography and Vascular Technology modalities are CAAHEP accredited. All modalities emphasize student-centered instruction oriented towards professional success. Facilities provide state-of-the-art imaging equipment, labs, simulators, and the latest technology to prepare learners to be leaders in the field. The medical imaging faculty are an amazing team and part of a tradition of excellence at Oregon Tech.<br><br>The MIT department has faculty openings in four modalities. The Radiologic Science program seeks applicants with registries in CT, MRI and/or Interventional radiography. The Nuclear Medicine program seeks applicants holding certification in Nuclear Medicine from the ARRT or NMTCB. The Diagnostic Medical Sonography program seeks applicants with registries in breast, musculoskeletal, pediatrics and fetal echo. The Echocardiography program seeks applicants with registries in adult and pediatric echo.<br><br></div><div>The primary focus of all faculty positions in the MIT department is on excellent teaching at the bachelor’s level. The successful candidate’s instructional responsibilities will include a variety of core courses in one of the modalities depending upon certification/credentials, and experience. Faculty are expected to advise students, improve courses through continuous assessment, and adjust content to reflect current workforce trends.</div><div><br></div><div>Tenure-track faculty must establish a scholarly record and meet all tenure requirements. Scholarship at Oregon Tech takes a variety of forms, including but not limited to applied research that engages students, conference presentations to disseminate best practices or field experience, or authorship of peer-reviewed publications. Faculty are expected to participate in institutional (department and university) and professional service. Faculty will pursue professional development to stay current in the discipline and enhance instructional practices.<br><br>We are pleased to offer competitive incentives to the successful candidate upon hire. Additional information will be provided to the selected candidate.<br><br>REQUIREMENTS<br>The position requires a master’s degree in medical imaging, higher education, or related field with a bachelor’s degree in a medical imaging modality. Doctorate degree is preferred.<br><br>Applicants should have current certification/credentials and minimum of five years of related occupational work experience. Applicants should have teaching experience at the college level and/or in industry training experience, and ability to establish a (or established) record of scholarly activities. Applicants should indicate modality preferred based upon certification/credentials, and experience in their cover letter.</div> Medical Imaging Technology https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/6756 2024-12-13T14:04:29-08:00 2024-12-13T14:04:30-08:00 Campus Safety Officer (Temporary, On-Call) <div>Campus Safety invites applications for Temporary, On-Call - Campus Safety Officers.<br><br>The purpose of this position is to maintain order and the safety of persons and property on the Oregon Tech campus by enforcing the University, state, city and federal rules, regulations and policies relating to the safety and protection of students, staff, faculty and visitors. This is accomplished through emergency response, prevention and investigation of crimes and violations of federal and state laws along with university policies and detaining of offenders.<br><br>The Campus Safety Officer also provides the campus community with instruction and training when required and enforces Oregon Tech parking policies.<br><br>Incumbent shall maintain broad availability to work hours across all shifts and times to backfill and/or supplement uniform operations as deemed necessary by the Director – Campus Safety (i.e., athletic/special events, vacancies, vacations, sick time, etc.). This position requires that the incumbent shall be consistently responsive to all work requests some of which may be communicated with minimal or no advanced notice.</div> Security https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7398 2026-05-21T12:32:40-07:00 2026-05-21T12:32:40-07:00 Director - Environmental Health and Safety <div>The Director – Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) is a key leadership position within Resilience, Emergency Management and Safety (REMS). This position is responsible for managing the university’s environmental health and safety portfolio ensuring compliance with applicable regulations and implementing practices to mitigate safety-related risks. The Director – EHS routinely collaborates with stakeholders to develop a sustainable culture of regulatory compliance, resilience, risk mitigation and safety.</div><div><br></div><div>The Director – EHS manages assigned budgets, personnel, programs and resources. This position is responsible for conducting strategic planning, developing programs and services, and advancing the concept of organizational resilience throughout the university. The position is accountable for safety programs and services across the university to include the Klamath Falls, Portland-Metro and Scappoose campuses. This position serves as a standing member on the university's Radiation Safety Committee and Safety Commission.</div> Environmental Health/Safety Office https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/7071 2025-08-08T11:03:28-07:00 2025-08-08T11:03:29-07:00 Adjunct Instructor, Anthropology/Archeology <div>Oregon Tech is accepting applications for Anthropology undergraduate Adjunct Instructors for the Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) Department.<br><br></div><div>The Humanities and Social Sciences Department is recruiting a pool of adjunct instructors for possible part-time teaching positions to support the department's General Education courses. Specifically, the department seeks adjunct instructors to teach: Globalization, Cultural Anthropology, Physical Anthropology and/or Archeology. Qualified applicants may be invited to serve as adjunct instructors for courses within the department.<br><br></div><div><strong>Teaching Modality:</strong> Appointments may include courses offered on-line, in-person on-campus, hybrid, or related lab; or in an alternative format responsive to state and local requirements.<br><br></div><div><strong>Location: </strong>The primary campus locations include the Klamath Falls campus, the Portland-Metro campus (located in Wilsonville, OR), and online. Teaching may be conducted remotely/online, within the United States.<br><br>Interested candidates should apply to the posting through the posting on the Oregon Tech Job Board, and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with contact information. In your cover letter, please specify those areas or courses that you are qualified to offer and would be interested in teaching.<br><br></div><div>This pool will be accessed only when an opening or need arises. Your credentials will remain active as long as the pool position is available; but no more than two years. After two years, if you are still interested, you must reapply to the most current adjunct pool.</div> Humanities and Social Sciences"
    },
