    "https://jobs.oit.edu/postings/6928": {
      "title": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing &amp; Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET)",
      "description": "Oregon Institute of Technology Portal | Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing &amp; Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQs Campus Locations Human Resources Oregon Tech Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing & Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit an application and include the following elements: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document Posting Details Position Details Position Type Adjunct Working Title Adjunct Instructor Pool, Manufacturing & Mechanical Engineering Technology (MMET) Classification Title Adjunct Faculty College/Division College of Engr, Tech & Mgmt (ETM) Department Manufacturing & Mechanical Eng Tech Hiring Unit Work Location Appointment FTE (%) Position Terms/Mo Full/Part time Annual Salary Based on WLU Position Summary Department Summary Manufacturing Engineering Technology The objective of the Manufacturing Engineering Technology undergraduate program is to offer students a quality education that provides the greatest possible opportunity for rewarding and successful careers. This includes practical training and technical education in engineering, manufacturing processes, and manufacturing equipment as well as supplemental coursework in communications, mathematics, science, social science, and business. Mechanical Engineering The Mechanical Engineering Program at Oregon Institute of Technology provides an excellent theoretical and applied or hands on engineering education. The program provides graduates with a foundation in fundamentals, applications, design, project management, communications, and professional and ethical responsibility. Mechanical Engineering Technology The objective of the Mechanical Engineering Technology Program is to ensure that graduates of this curriculum acquire competency in those theoretical, applied engineering and practical subjects necessary to become successful in their careers. The program strives to maintain a reputation for academic standards that will assure graduates a welcome by prospective employers. https://www.oit.edu/mmet Position Summary The Department of Manufacturing and Mechanical Engineering Technology at Oregon Institute of Technology (Oregon Tech) is seeking applications for a part-time adjunct faculty pool for the 2025-2026 academic year. These positions will be based at the Portland-Metro campus in Wilsonville and will be offered on a term-by-term basis. Renewals may be considered annually at the discretion of the department chair. Adjunct faculty will be responsible for developing and/or teaching undergraduate courses within the Manufacturing and Mechanical Engineering Technology department, which is part of the College of Engineering, Technology, and Management at Oregon Tech. Courses that may require instructors include: Automation and Robotics Programmable Logic Controllers (PLCs) Control Systems Materials Science and Engineering Mechanical Vibrations Electric Power Systems Machining Processes Manufacturing Tool Design Computer-Aided Design ( CAD ) / Computer-Aided Manufacturing ( CAM ) Minimum Requirements Additional Requirements Proven track record of teaching engineering courses. Education must include (at least) a Master’s degree in an engineering discipline by the start date of employment. Successful candidates must hold permanent, full-time, US Work Authorization. Preferred Qualifications PhD in an engineering dicipline. Application Information Recruitment Type External Application Screening Begins 05/07/2025 Job Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicant Please submit an application and include the following elements: Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document Background/Pre-Employment Check Any offer of employment to a successful candidate will be conditioned upon the University’s receipt of a satisfactory background check, motor vehicle check, physical abilities check, and/or any other conditions of employment contained in the vacancy announcement. AA/EEO Statement Oregon Tech is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Educator and Employer. The University does not discriminate in access to its educational programs and activities, or with respect to hiring, or the terms and conditions of employment, on the basis of age, color, disability, marital status, national origin, race, religion or creed, sex or gender, gender identity or gender expression, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other basis in law. Oregon Tech is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Office of Human Resource at 541-885-1028 or oithr@oit.edu . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Transcripts (Unofficial) Teaching Philosophy License/Certification Other Document Contact Us: Office of Human Resources 3201 Campus Dr. Klamath Falls, Oregon 97601 Phone: (541) 885-1120 Email: oithr@oit.edu Website: http://www.oit.edu/hr Policies | Campus Safety | Campus Alerts | Directory | Site Index Connect with us: | | To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
